Z||000000||pHoOl||01-05-2001||11:07 PM||||I've been having an idea of making a forum similar to this for a book exchange at my university.  I've noticed that a lot of the forums use a similar software package (everything looks the same).  Could you tell me what the software is called?  and possibly where i can buy it or download it?<P>thanks much,<BR>matt<P>------------------<BR>AIM: phool88fiero<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||LarryB||01-06-2001||12:40 AM||||That's easy. The software package is known as the Ultimate Bulletin Board (UBB) and the vendor is at <A HREF="http://www.infopop.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.infopop.com</A> <P>The full licensed version (which is what Cliff is using) is $200 which includes a year of software upgrades.<P>There is also a free very-limited-functionality version as well. <P>You'd be hard-pressed to find a much better commercial product for $200, and at that price most people would be crazy to write their own package. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||pHoOl||01-06-2001||12:47 AM||||How crippled is the free download?  i think i'll download and try it.  <P>------------------<BR>AIM: phool88fiero<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||LarryB||01-06-2001||09:42 AM||||From memory you can't set up an email address in your user profile, you're limited to something like 9 forums, you're a lot more restricted in your ability to tweak the interface, you can't lock down topics, and there's other stuff that I don't remember.  <P>The application is mostly CGI scripts so <BR>you also need to be running a web server that has perl v5 on it (5.003 or later?).  <BR>I used a Sun running Solaris 2.6 with Apache and UBB ran out of the box with a couple of minor tweaks (internal application at work) and I had a usable site up in less than an hour. <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||01-06-2001||01:31 PM||||It's written in Perl... I've looked into it for a coupe things myself. You need a really good server for it. Otherwise forget searches. they will take forever. like they did here untill Cliff replaced the server a few months ago.<P>It can live on either NT/IIS or Linux/Apache. It requires Perl 5 be installed before the forum software. <P>You need to know the server well before installing the forum. If you botch it you'll have all kinds of security holes. It won't be long before it gets hacked if you don't setup the server right.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Songman||01-06-2001||05:12 PM||||I've been using UBB for quite a while in a couple of places. I love it. I know none of the freebie site places like GeoCities will run it but I have never had any trouble on any of my others...<P>I did have a couple of problems when I set up my first board but the UBB support forum is great and they helped me get going in no time!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
